{
  "id": "refresh-token-race-two-tabs",
  "title": "Two tabs refresh the same token: timeline of the race",
  "persona": "A frontend engineer chasing random logouts in a single-page app, drawing what they think happens when two open tabs refresh the session at the same moment.",
  "topic": "why users get logged out when two tabs refresh the token at once",
  "realism": "Race conditions are almost always whiteboarded as lanes with time running left to right; the order of events lives only in their horizontal position, and people mark 'the moment it breaks' with a vertical line and circle the overlap window rather than drawing arrows between the two lanes.",
